{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/439682-what-does-your-totem-do-when-your-wolves-aren-t-bothering-it","id":439682,"title":"What does your totem do when your wolves aren't bothering it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-13T03:47:53-07:00","id":439682,"title":"What does your totem do when your wolves aren't bothering it?","content":"<br /> Rosekill is a budding magath. A small little spirit of bullying born in the shadow of the sorority dorm. Every year when rush comes around, Rosekill and its siblings gather in a feeding frenzy to grow on the pain, embarrassment and alienation. And even the little tender bits of glowing hope crushed. <br /> <br /> Rosekill got its jump in growth when one of the pledges hung herself. So now Rosekill's got a taste for suicide, and a mission. <br /> <br /> As far as totems go, Rosekill isn't ideal. But it (she) bullied and wheedled a most unusual pack of one lonely wolf into accepting her. <br /> <br /> I like to think of her lurking around the dorms during the day, encouraging the girls to do terrible things to one another, and themselves. &quot;Tell her she's fat!&quot; &quot;Kiss her boyfriend!&quot; &quot;Make her clean all the toilets!&quot; &quot;Puke up your lunch!&quot; &quot;Cut off your ugly ears!&quot;<br /> <br /> When possible, she jumps into the bodies of the coed's themselves and is happy to spend weeks breeding a culture of cruelty in the flesh. <br /> <br /> Otherwise, I imagine that as a growing spirit in her hierachy, and with the benefit of becoming a magath, she's developing a wider world view, in a spirit sense, and is frequently travelling to seek out the powers that be who can extend her influence. <br /> <br /> So a question - what do you imagine your totems doing all day, when they're not being bothered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T05:13:59-07:00","id":439782,"title":"","content":"I think of the Hisil like an ecosystem. Pretend you are watching a nature documentary or a fish tank. When you aren't stomping around being an alpha predator the spirits are adapting to the slowly-morphing terrain (effected greatly by human interactions and emotions) and basically preying on one another. The spirits that are defining characteristics of a place are big and strong while the ones they feed on are footnotes.<br /> <br /> Roseluck feeds on spirits of schedule and experimentation and independence and homework and the clumsiness that starts popcorn fires and the sloth that comes from staying up late on the weekends - things that are in EVERY college. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T07:21:51-07:00","id":439852,"title":"","content":"The usual answer is get more essence.<br /> <br /> But depending on its rank, it might be out and about doing politics. I think the rank where it develops its own identity is 3, offhand, but at that point it may start currying lesser spirits, doling out essence to them so that they will serve it. It might also try finding a place among the courts of higher ranked spirits of similar Resonance, or the location, which will probably stretch beyond the dorm and to the entire university. It might try to find a locus, too, especially one that others may have overlooked, perhaps due to it being in an 'unappetizing' area, like a Wound. If it hasn't gained its own personality yet, it might be used as a tool by higher ranked spirits to further their own ends.<br /> <br /> A big thing to keep in mind, though, is if it's a magath, it will probably be excluded from the spirit politics. I'm not sure to what extent, but it does seem like magath are sort of shunned by 'regular' spirits, which can make it difficult to operate if they won't let it hang out near the bigger loci. However, it also opens up opportunities. If your magath hasn't developed its own personality yet, it can act as more of a mad dog, gathering up other spirits and possibly more influences. If it has, it may start plotting against the existing spirits to sort of assure that its own influences are fed. This might mean, for example, trying to taint the resonance of certain areas, maybe getting rid of certain key spirits at the schools' mental health facility, or if it's stuck to the dorm, trying to get rid of restraint, possibly by driving off the spirit of the sorority, which probably watches over the girls there and keeps things from deviating too far from normal.<br /> <br /> It would probably try and encourage its Uratha to expand its pack, not just with other Uratha but wolf-blooded and humans too, so they could turn smaller incidents of bullying into larger things, or be bullies themselves. Occasionally people die in werewolf hunts, and making those deaths appear to be suicides might be a good way to get some appropriate essence for that kind of thing flowing.<br /> <br /> You posted about the internet spirits. If there was a computer lab nearby it might be a good hunting ground for a spirit of bullying to get some essence and devour some lesser spirits of its kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T11:25:01-07:00","id":440186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/439682-what-does-your-totem-do-when-your-wolves-aren-t-bothering-it?p=439852#post439852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The usual answer is get more essence.<br /> <br /> But depending on its rank, it might be out and about doing politics. I think the rank where it develops its own identity is <b>3</b>,</div> </div> </div> </div>Rank 2, actually. (No, I still haven't assimilated the new terms.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T11:36:08-07:00","id":440202,"title":"","content":"I just checked, it's rank 3. The Hursihim, Ensihim and so forth are made up of two ranks each, an -ih and an -ah, each referring to a different rank, which is the tricky part.<br /> <br /> Rank 0 is the Muthra, who are just dormant.<br /> Rank 1 is the Hursih, rank 2 are the Hursah, who are animals and children in the spiritual heirarchy.<br /> Then Rank 3 is the Ensih, the 'fully independent spirits, evolved beyond their ties to a single source of Essence. They make up most of the spirits involved with Hisil politics, furthering the agendas of their umia.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T13:58:59-07:00","id":440444,"title":"","content":"Funny, back in first edition said independence started at rank 2, and was thus why most Forsaken totems had that rank. Guess nowadays is rank 3 for most Forsaken totems and 4 for most Pure ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T14:27:10-07:00","id":440467,"title":"","content":"Speaking of totem and rank, for a starting 4 or 5 member pack straight out of chargen, does it make sense to invest in a stronger totem? Not just mechanically, but thematically or narratively? I suppose it depends on the spirit (and the ST) but I would wonder if the requests and needs of a bigger spirit just aren't too much for a fresh group to handle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T14:36:57-07:00","id":440481,"title":"","content":"What did you guys' totems do when not working for the pack? We never got one in our last game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T14:42:31-07:00","id":440489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/439682-what-does-your-totem-do-when-your-wolves-aren-t-bothering-it?p=440467#post440467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of totem and rank, for a starting 4 or 5 member pack straight out of chargen, does it make sense to invest in a stronger totem? Not just mechanically, but thematically or narratively? I suppose it depends on the spirit (and the ST) but I would wonder if the requests and needs of a bigger spirit just aren't too much for a fresh group to handle?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would be a pretty cool theme for a chronicle. Also, it could be a totem that was inherited from the 'old guard' of the territory","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T14:51:04-07:00","id":440494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/439682-what-does-your-totem-do-when-your-wolves-aren-t-bothering-it?p=440481#post440481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did you guys' totems do when not working for the pack? We never got one in our last game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never had one period! That's why I ask :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T18:20:01-07:00","id":440717,"title":"","content":"Here is the story of the Raven..<br /> It used to remember some of its kind back in the early days, but they changed into something called &quot;Halaku&quot;.<br /> Fihir Crum did not. He instead studied the strange Uratha from a distance. How they move and shift. how they work and how they communicate.<br /> It built a cover as something weak and useful for a pack in need of a totem.<br /> Even though they would never trust him fully, he knew they needed him. Of course they did. And he was happy to oblige.<br /> He just had to be careful to approach them in a way that they would not expect what he is.<br /> He spoke to one of the young wolf blooded. many a time. The Wolf Blooded seemed eager to learn more about spirits. So it asked the young being to let Fihir Crum help the Wolves in the pack.<br /> Every time they don't see, it is secretly spying on the pack. Making sure it has enough dirt on everyone so they dont evict it when the wolves find out what it is.<br /> Fihir Crum does not know all the details. it does not want to remember it all. It wants the lie to continue. Maybe the wolves can hunt down and kill all those pesky Halaku and those spirits that knows?<br /> Every chance it has Fihir Crum steals something. it has to steal something from the pack and does not always want to let go when the theft is found out.<br /> Fihir Crum does not mean to lie to the pack from time to time. It just lies in its nature to do so. Sometimes it is for the best. So it hides and waits, hoping that the pack will protect it while Fihir Crum looks to evolve again..<br /> And so it goes..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T19:33:59-07:00","id":440792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephraim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/439682-what-does-your-totem-do-when-your-wolves-aren-t-bothering-it?p=440717#post440717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is the story of the Raven..<br /> It used to remember some of its kind back in the early days, but they changed into something called &quot;Halaku&quot;.<br /> Fihir Crum did not. He instead studied the strange Uratha from a distance. How they move and shift. how they work and how they communicate.<br /> It built a cover as something weak and useful for a pack in need of a totem.<br /> Even though they would never trust him fully, he knew they needed him. Of course they did. And he was happy to oblige.<br /> He just had to be careful to approach them in a way that they would not expect what he is.<br /> He spoke to one of the young wolf blooded. many a time. The Wolf Blooded seemed eager to learn more about spirits. So it asked the young being to let Fihir Crum help the Wolves in the pack.<br /> Every time they don't see, it is secretly spying on the pack. Making sure it has enough dirt on everyone so they dont evict it when the wolves find out what it is.<br /> Fihir Crum does not know all the details. it does not want to remember it all. It wants the lie to continue. Maybe the wolves can hunt down and kill all those pesky Halaku and those spirits that knows?<br /> Every chance it has Fihir Crum steals something. it has to steal something from the pack and does not always want to let go when the theft is found out.<br /> Fihir Crum does not mean to lie to the pack from time to time. It just lies in its nature to do so. Sometimes it is for the best. So it hides and waits, hoping that the pack will protect it while Fihir Crum looks to evolve again..<br /> And so it goes..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awesome. Reading up on spirits tonight to flesh out RoseKill. Good inspiration there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T19:47:47-07:00","id":440803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephraim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/439682-what-does-your-totem-do-when-your-wolves-aren-t-bothering-it?p=440717#post440717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is the story of the Raven..</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that game loosely based on Teen Wolf, the tv series?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T08:16:58-07:00","id":441332,"title":"","content":"I see our pack's totem - <b>Wary-Nest</b>, a spirit of home and vigilance that appears as a <a href=\"http://www.adventurecloud.com/img/s3/v43/p479320971-3.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Kea</a> - spending most of its time watching over its territory in Twilight and in the Shadow. It is a worried little thing, overly-concerned with security, and I would expect it to scare off any humans that approach (I'm seeing a poor door-knocking energy company salesman running off in panic when he hears ephemeral squarking or feels phantom talons tracing down his back), and to chase off or eat any spirits that look like they might cause trouble in the Hisil. It is very pleased to have joined a pack, because the Wolves now let it into Flesh to better look after its home.<br /> <br /> It's also taken to one of the Wolf-Blooded pack members, a school-aged kid who has the Waystone Tell. A little more than the kid's mother (my character) would like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T10:45:54-07:00","id":441575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/439682-what-does-your-totem-do-when-your-wolves-aren-t-bothering-it?p=441332#post441332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see our pack's totem - <b>Wary-Nest</b>, a spirit of home and vigilance that appears as a <a href=\"http://www.adventurecloud.com/img/s3/v43/p479320971-3.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Kea</a> - spending most of its time watching over its territory in Twilight and in the Shadow. It is a worried little thing, overly-concerned with security, and I would expect it to scare off any humans that approach (I'm seeing a poor door-knocking energy company salesman running off in panic when he hears ephemeral squarking or feels phantom talons tracing down his back), and to chase off or eat any spirits that look like they might cause trouble in the Hisil. It is very pleased to have joined a pack, because the Wolves now let it into Flesh to better look after its home.<br /> <br /> It's also taken to one of the Wolf-Blooded pack members, a school-aged kid who has the Waystone Tell. A little more than the kid's mother (my character) would like.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A busybody totem of security sounds like a good ally to have. <br /> <br /> I decided that since RoseKill is a budding magath, she's being shunned by most of the local spirits. And so she's begun to search far and wide for something, some group. or someone to ally herself with. I have some guesses on who she might find, or how she might pursue it. <br /> <br /> Tonight is the first game night *fingers crossed*. Fully expecting some bumps but excited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T15:10:38-07:00","id":441871,"title":"","content":"Good luck! She's definitely creepy; I'm sure she'll go far. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T17:55:34-07:00","id":442019,"title":"","content":"Do packs in forsaken not need totems like they do in apocalypse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T18:08:20-07:00","id":442044,"title":"","content":"The don't strictly need them to just say 'we're a pack', but to count as one mechanically they need a Totem. Fortunately in Second Edition every werewolf at character generation starts with a free dot in the Totem merit, so there's even less reason not to have one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T07:24:58-07:00","id":444173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/439682-what-does-your-totem-do-when-your-wolves-aren-t-bothering-it?p=440803#post440803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was that game loosely based on Teen Wolf, the tv series?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, Have not seen that one.<br /> <br /> Fihir Crum was actually inspired of the &quot;predators&quot; 1E WtF book.<br /> We found some stuff there that we patched together to give the totem a strange and scattered backstory.<br /> We basically wrote him up as one of the first of his kind.<br /> A carrion prince, a thief and a liar.<br /> He would have been very powerful as a spirit but was decieved by his own kind.<br /> Now he &quot;serves&quot; the Uratha, while he tries to get them to find what he is looking for.<br /> <br /> He might be driven by a desire for revenge, but he is mostly a spirit that has lost itself in its own vices. It loves to steal, cheat, lie and bullshit those around him.<br /> When the PC gets fooled or allows the totem to trick or fool the pack I give the player in question a beat. Every time.<br /> It has lead to some interesting stories so far.<br /> <br /> We had a story last week based on the concept of this thread actually.<br /> <br /> Fun times.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T16:13:29-07:00","id":445047,"title":"","content":"Think up ways to bother and create trouble for their pack is my guess. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T13:36:24-07:00","id":454800,"title":"","content":"I feel like a totem spirit starts off usually as a slightly disdainful ally, and slowly grows to appreciate the pack. In a general sense. Remember, the pack offers it protection, belonging, power, and the most important thing: essence. They also act as resonant and I'm not sure if it is this way now, but can be used as anchors and such allowing the spirit to hang out on the flesh side for however long it wants. There are a lot of benefits, with the major detriments being: gotta help now and again, get kind of boned in spirit politics, make new enemies, and of course the good ol, not every pack is nice to its totem. <br /> <br /> The pack totem in our game is a Highway Cat from Predators. An arrogant jerk, he likes to push pack members to drive fast and crazy, and steal fast, expensive cars. He hates sitting around, and doesn't like other things respected more than himself. However, like a pet cat, he has the tendency to step in and help in dire circumstances because he likes have a food dish that fills itself (ie. not having to hunt spirits or defend a locus, but siphon it from the werewolves presence and the chiminage, is it still called that? that they offer)<br /> <br /> Examples, jumping between pack members to warn of issues, influencing cars to increase their handling and speed, and hunting with the Hunter in Darkness in the Hisil. It likes to hunt small car spirits like Beetles, Fiestas and Darts. <br /> <br /> As to what they do on their free time? Highway Cat likes to run along the roads, and patrol its grounds. It loves to lay around doing nothing, that's always good. It has begun to create its own court in the territory of spirits associated with cars (its a Sports Car spirit). So small computer, communication, greed, car, fire, metal, glass, happiness, anger spirits all fit in that list. It hunts them down and adds them to its 'line up'. It is trying to compete with the spirit that controls one of the Loci that the pack barters with, and some of the building spirits that have accumulated small fiefs and armies of lesser spirits. <br /> <br /> I like to think of the spirit world as a sort of tribal land. There are stragglers about, and the big ones build little micro tribes around key geographic areas, usually a locus or a site that generates a lot of essence. Those same sites can just as easily be swarmed feeding frenzies of little spirits, such as a pack's abandoned locus (when the Pure killed half the pack and chased off the others), which is quickly swarmed with little spirit like flies on a rotting carcass. <br /> <br /> Just some thoughts. <br /> <br /> How do you describe the spirit's relationship with the pack?<br /> <br /> Do you enter the Hisil a lot? I have a hard time picturing it well. Anyway have a description? We're in Chicago, so very urban.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T13:58:19-07:00","id":454812,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/73/The_Wire_Bubbles.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I've always viewed Totems as on treats you're trusted CI in an area. Hence how the police used Bubbles in the Wire.<br /> <br /> When it's not being bothered by the Pack, it does what spirits do. It collects essence, engages in Choir politicking, and generally acts according to it's nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}